# ESP32-S3 N16R8 dev board without a screen (YD-ESP32-S3 N16R8, ESP32-S3-CAM
# N16R8, ESP32-S3-DevKitC-1 N16R8). Two USB-C ports:
#   "USB"/"OTG": the chip's own USB, becomes the printer's host
#   "COM"/"TTL": USB-UART chip (CH343/CP2102) on UART0, for flashing and the log
# BOOT (GPIO0): press = scan, twice = test page. RGB LED (WS2812) on GPIO48.
CONFIG_PRINT_BUTTON2_GPIO=-1
CONFIG_USER_BUTTON_GPIO=-1
CONFIG_LCD_NV3023=n
# flashed over the COM/TTL port: a short window is enough
CONFIG_USB_HOST_DELAY_S=3
CONFIG_USB_MODE_BUTTON_A_GPIO=-1
CONFIG_USB_MODE_BUTTON_B_GPIO=-1
